ng of the walls was URI rice this  means that had Grisha gone down into the  basement that day he would have ended up  fighting him instead of Frida and it's  feasible the fight might have ended  differently after all URI was shown to  have lightning fast reflexes during his  encounter with Kenny Ackerman and at  this time he would have had a shifter  for around six or seven years making him  far more experienced than Freda was when  she was defeated  another piece of trivia was that in this  memory when Grisha discovered the map to  the rice Chapel he then crossed Paws  with Kenny who was now being employed by  the royal family had Kenny found out  what he was hiding in his pocket then  there's a sort of chance he might have  tried to slice his neck which may or may  not have led to Grisha turning into a  Titan so it's just a good thing for  everyone that he was able to leave  without being questioned  now moving on to one of the best scenes  in the episode we see that Grisha fell  asleep in his basement while writing one  of his famous books in his sleep he  starts to receive memories from the  future that belong to present-day Aaron  and we're gonna pause for a second to  explain what exactly is going on  to start things off it's fairly normal  for a Time shift to see memories that  belong to a previous user but when it  comes to Holders of the attack Titan  these guys are sometimes able to see  memories from their future inheritors as  well one example is how back in season 3  Kruger told his successor to save Mikasa  and Armin despite neither of them being  born yet and now in this new episode a  similar thing happens again because  Aaron and his dad are both holders of  the attack Titan Grisha from the pass is  therefore able to see memories that  belong to Aaron in the future in this  specific scene notice how when Aaron  looks down at this picture of Zeke his  dad then immediately reacts and  apologizes to his first son then when  present-day Aaron looks directly at his  raggedy bearded brother Grisha from the  past reacts again as he sees a vision of  a bearded man who he recognizes as Zeke  what this shows is that thanks to his  attack Titan Grisha can occasionally see  the future through Aaron's point of view  and as the video continues we'll break  down how this ability enables them to  communicate through time  anyway after seeing everything so far  Zeke finally realizes that his  assumptions were wrong and their father  didn't bring much Aaron to become an  alien restorationist because of this  Zeke begins to wonder why Aaron then  betrayed him and acts the way he does  since he's doing all the things his  father would have wanted only without  ever being told to do so Aaron goes on  to explain that no one had to make him  this way and that since birth he's just  always had this drive to protect his own  Freedom no matter what the cost in this  memory here we get a look at the crime  scene after Aaron and Mikasa killed  those kidnappers and it was kind of  funny seeing Zeke and his dad react in  the same way this moment here emphasized  just how different the two Jaeger Bros  are since Zeke's backstory made it clear  that he was content to live a life  inside the internment Zone whereas by  contrast Aaron is someone who felt  confined by the walls and was quite  literally willing to kill people who  threatened his freedom  with this difference in character now  being established you might then be  wondering why is he continued to take  them through their dad's memories and  the answer is that he still believed he  could change Aaron's mind in the same  way that Sava once saved him he is now  desperate to save Aaron and so he's not  going to carry out the euthanization  plan until he finds at least one memory  that might change his brother's  perspective  as they walk through flashback off the  flashback we get moments that are subtly  relevant to things that Grisha says  later in the episode for example in this  