ntally  it also happened to be the same day the  Warriors attacked this coincidence was  confirmed later in the episode when he  spells out that he didn't know which day  the wars were going to be destroyed  switching back to the memory in question  we then get a replay of the scene where  he promises to show Aaron what's in the  basement this time around the camera  pans out to reveal Aaron's standing  there watching the moment Play Out and  because of grisha's future memory  inheritance he feels the presence in  front of him again just like he did in  the basement he then makes his final  Journey to the rice Chapel almost a  decade after he first attempted to  confront them and this sequence was  undeniably the best part of the episode  as he begs Frida to save the people of  the Island from the Titans outside the  walls you can see that she does  genuinely have some concern for what  he's saying since the real Frida rice  wanted to save Humanity on parodies  however it wasn't long until she was  overtaken by the will of Carl Fritz who  began ranting about how eldian should  accept their fate because if they die it  means that fewer people outside the  walls have to suffer  this way of thinking is very similar to  Zeke which is why he had no complaints  about what she said but on the other  hand Aaron was getting angrier and  angrier as she kept talking remember  this memory is taking place on the same  day his mother was eaten by a Titan and  here you have someone trying to justify  her death and the death of everyone else  who was killed by The Warriors his  intense feelings of Rage could be felt  by his dad in the past hence why he  reacts in this moment and it's about  time we break this moment down step by  step Point number one is that when this  really happened all those years ago  Chris's attack Titan enabled him to  receive memories from this version of  Aaron the memories he received in this  scene were essentially a live stream  from Aaron's perspective