o walk by they wouldn't  actually see Zeke in fact all they see  is Grisha hugging thin air but because  we're seeing this in the past Dimension  it gives off a powerful illusion that  this is really happening of course it  needs to be said that this is only  possible because of the attack Titan's  power since if their dad had any other  shifter then he wouldn't be able to see  the future through Aaron's eyes this  emotional moment was enough physique to  acknowledge Grisha as his dad because  we've known all along that he wanted his  fatherly love and the reason he had all  this hatred inside him is since he never  truly received it until now  finally the biggest remaining question  coming out of this episode is why would  Grisha still give Aaron the attack Titan  if he didn't want the terrible future he  saw to happen this is a mystery that has  at least three separate valid reasons  and yeah I'm gonna start with the one  that's the most obvious during this  scene when he asked Zeke to stop Aaron  Grisha had no idea that earlier that day  his wife had been eaten by a Titan if we  flash forward to the moment he finds out  his expression completely changes and  the first words he says are that Aaron  needs to avenge his mother Grisha knows  more than anyone on the island that  Malia the ones responsible for  destroying the walls but with his time  as the attack Titan running out the only  person who can avenge Carla is Aaron  this brings us to reason number two  which is that due to the curse of Emir  Grisha had to pass his shifter to  someone and he already established that  his son might be a good choice earlier  he realized that Aaron had a strong  desire to be free which is an integral  part of being the attack Titan and it's  why he was prepared to tell his son the  truth about the world  to put it simply if he didn't pass it to  Aaron then there was no one worthy that  he could pass it to and if he didn't  give it to anyone then there's a chance  to shifter would have fallen into  Molly's hands after his death since the  power would be inherited by a newborn  aldian anywhere in the world he must  have figured it was a safer option to  give it to his son and hopefully in the  future things can work themselves out  finally the third reason he chose to  make this decision is that not doing so  would have created a paradox since  Grisha already knows that future Aaron  possesses the attack Titan if he  willingly chose to avoid his future then  he had no idea what would have happened  I mean for all he knows he might have  started fading away because if Aaron  never gets the attack Titan then future  Aaron wouldn't have been there to  motivate Grisha in the chapel either way  Grisha had no way of knowing what would  happen if he didn't follow the  predetermined path so this is likely a  factor in why he did what he did  anyway people that was my breakdown for  episode 20 of Attack on Titan season 4  and I hope you clear some things up as  the shifter abilities can get super  confusing if you enjoyed the video then  I'd appreciate if you hit that sub  button and let me know in the comments  what you thought of the episode until  the next one peace out

